repository-code: "https://github.com/Apsiape/finite-contact-theory-public"
abstract: "A public release of Finite Contact Theory, a long-range finite reconstruction program. This v0.6 chapter ships the program's experimental face: a complete, dependency-free public implementation of the driven one-use generative floor dynamics (exactly specified, with replay and maximally-coupled counterfactual modes) and three measured phenomena with pre-stated fences: the drive manufactures indistinguishable twins and 92.7% separate before world end (independent-implementation agreement with the private laboratory engine); separation waits are exponential-form, decisively beating a power law; and redirecting a single fork choice under an identical random stream produces an edge-set defect growing linearly at 1.25 edges per contact (R^2 = 0.998). All measurements are counting observables; one private result (the redundancy-engine inversion) is cited and explicitly not claimed at public scale."
version: "0.6.0"
date-released: "2026-07-13"
